<%# The handover form for a `github` universe: one optional message from the author
    # and one submit, posting to `drafts#submit`.
    #
    # **It is a form rather than a `button_to` because the message cannot travel on
    # a button.** An optional field and a bare control are two different shapes of
    # the same decision, and the reviewer's approval already found this out in slice
    # 5.2: a note that has to be typed cannot ride in a `data:` attribute or survive
    # a confirmation dialog. `Draft#submit!` writes the message onto the request it
    # creates, so the field is a parameter of a submission rather than a column an
    # author edits — a rejected draft comes back as working work and the next
    # handover gets its own message.
    #
    # **It renders only while the draft is a working one** (`draft?`, not `open?`),
    # because a draft that is already with a reviewer has nothing left to hand over
    # and one that is closed has nothing at all. A control that would be refused is
    # worse than no control, which is the same rule the page header follows.
    #
    # The section rather than a button also gives the mode's sentence somewhere to
    # live: a `wikipedia` author pressing **Apply changes** needs nothing explained,
    # and a `github` author pressing **Submit for review** needs to know that nothing
    # is written yet and that somebody else decides. %>
<section class="surface-card p-4 mt-3 draft-submission">
  <h2 class="h5"><%= t("drafts.submission.heading") %></h2>
  <p class="page-description"><%= t("drafts.submission.lead") %></p>

  <%= form_with(url: submit_universe_draft_path(id: draft), method: :post,
    class: "draft-submission-form") do %>
    <%= label_tag "submission_message", t("drafts.submission.message"), class: "form-label" %>
    <%= text_area_tag "review_request[submission_message]", nil, rows: 3,
      id: "submission_message", class: "form-control" %>
    <p class="page-description"><%= t("drafts.submission.message_hint") %></p>

    <div class="page-actions d-flex align-items-center flex-wrap gap-2 mt-3">
      <%= submit_tag t("drafts.submission.submit"), class: "btn btn-primary" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>